<BaseLayout title="Repairs and DIY">
  <h1>Repairs and DIY</h1>
  <p>This library is organized around practical jobs: identify the correct configuration, prepare the vehicle, confirm parts and tools, follow a verified procedure, then inspect and document the result. A guide marked as an overview is not a complete workshop procedure.</p>
  <h2>Repair guides</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Guide</th><th>Scope</th><th>Risk / status</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th><a href="./front-brake-pads/">Front brake pads</a></th><td>Planning, fitment checks, tools, work sequence overview and inspection points.</td><td>Safety-critical; exact brake package and service data required.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="./brake-assembly/">Brake assembly overview</a></th><td>Rotor, pads, caliper and carrier identification.</td><td>Educational illustration, not an installation procedure.</td></tr>
      <tr><th><a href="./paint-scratches/">Paint scratch repair</a></th><td>Assess paint transfer, clear-coat damage, primer and exposed metal.</td><td>Low risk when using paint-safe materials and careful technique.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <h2>Before starting any job</h2>
  <ol>
    <li>Identify model year, engine badge, drivetrain, trim, market, production date and relevant option codes.</li>
    <li>Confirm the exact part numbers and revisions using VIN-specific parts information.</li>
    <li>Use the correct lifting points, rated stands and a level work surface. Never work beneath a vehicle supported only by a jack.</li>
    <li>Obtain the official torque values, tightening sequence, one-time-use hardware rules and reset/calibration steps for the exact repair.</li>
    <li>Photograph the original installation and keep removed parts organized.</li>
    <li>Perform the required post-repair checks before returning the vehicle to service.</li>
  </ol>
  <div class="note"><strong>Safety boundary:</strong> brakes, steering, suspension, airbags, seat-belt systems, fuel systems and high-voltage hybrid components can cause serious injury if serviced incorrectly. The T8 Recharge requires high-voltage training and isolation procedures. Stop and use a qualified technician whenever the correct procedure or equipment is unavailable.</div>
  <h2>2026 repair cost guide (U.S.)</h2>
  <p>Ranges below are for planning a shop visit on a 2021 S60. They are not guaranteed quotes and may differ by brake package, engine, trim, parts quality, labor rate and location. Some RepairPal figures exclude tax and fees.</p>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Repair</th><th>Estimated installed cost</th><th>Scope</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th>Brake pads</th><td>$290–$370</td><td>Pad replacement estimate; rotors and unusual brake packages cost extra.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Brake pads and rotors</th><td>$500–$900 per axle</td><td>Broad planning range; confirm exact rotor and caliper package.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Battery replacement</th><td>$390–$545</td><td>2021 S60 estimates; correct battery type and registration/programming may affect price.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Timing belt</th><td>$735–$1,000</td><td>Belt replacement estimate; related parts may be additional.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Wheel alignment</th><td>$145–$215</td><td>Alignment only; worn components are extra.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Paint scratch repair</th><td>$150–$600 for a localized professional repair</td><td>Planning range only; deep damage or full-panel repaint can be substantially more.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p class="photo-disclaimer">Published estimates: <a href="https://repairpal.com/estimator/volvo/s60/2021/brake-pad-replacement-cost">RepairPal brake pads</a>, <a href="https://repairpal.com/estimator/volvo/s60/2021/battery-replacement-cost">RepairPal battery</a>, <a href="https://repairpal.com/estimator/volvo/s60/2021/timing-belt-replacement-cost">RepairPal timing belt</a>, and <a href="https://repairpal.com/estimator/volvo/s60/2021/wheel-alignment-cost">RepairPal alignment</a>. Rotor, paint and other planning allowances are not VIN-specific published quotes.</p>

